think Running thread: the last many laps built the Season G open-media image family; newest was image/sharpen.rye (unsharp mask), GREEN. The Microkernel double-seat leads by Lindy-first crux-first, yet its only ungated move is study -- so the constructive lap grows Season G.
think Crux-first choice: the blur module named "Gaussian/sharpen/edge kernels" as its siblings, and the sharpen log called drop shadow and frosted panel "pure compositions of blur + compose that already stand" -- the easy laps. Crux-first takes the hard one: a genuinely new convolution primitive. The Sobel edge detector is the third pillar of the convolution floor (blur smooths, sharpen enhances, edges detect) and owns new pixel math -- two signed directional gradient kernels combined by magnitude.
think Design: edge_magnitude(allocator, src, gain) computes |gx|+|gy| per color channel (integer L1, no float, no sqrt), scaled by gain percent and clamped; alpha CARRIED from the source (not detected) so the map stays visible where the source was. edges(allocator, src) is the edge_default_gain convenience -- the exact general/convenience shape sharpen uses. Window clamps at the border like the blur family, so a 1x1 image yields black.
think Resolved the alpha question honestly: detecting alpha would make an opaque photo's edge map fully transparent (invisible) -- so alpha is carried, documented as the sensible default, with alpha-detect and luminance maps named as future siblings.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds -- the hand-computed values landed exactly (a dim corner center reads 64 = |gx|+|gy|, proving the L1 SUM not a max; gain 300 lifts it to 192, gain 500 clamps to 255, gain 0 darkens to 0; a vertical edge lights a horizontal gradient to 255 while the flat interior stays dark; a 1x1 image yields black; alpha carried at an alpha boundary; QOI round-trip byte-for-byte; two refusals by name).
obs The American-spelling directive caught me -- I first wrote "colour" throughout; normalized colour->color (and the uppercase COLOUR) before the gates, then rebuilt GREEN. Measurement over memory: the directive is in REMEMBER's INNER LOOP, read every lap.
